// Lent 2027 path: 40 sessions (Ash Wednesday Feb 10 to Holy Saturday Mar 27, Sundays skipped).
// Scripture: World English Bible, British Edition (public domain), from ebible.org USFM.
window.LENT = {"days": [{"day": 1, "date": "2027-02-10", "week": "Ash Wednesday week: Return to the Lord", "title": "Return to me", "ref": "Joel 2:12-14", "leadIn": "Lent begins with an invitation. Through Joel, God calls his people to return with their whole heart, and not with a show of sorrow. The reason is simple: God is gracious and merciful, slow to anger and abundant in loving kindness.", "prayer": "Gracious God, I come back to you today with what I have. Forgive what I have ignored. Teach me to turn toward you again. Amen.", "reflect": "What is one thing you want to turn back to God during these forty days?"}, {"day": 2, "date": "2027-02-11", "week": "Ash Wednesday week: Return to the Lord", "title": "Create in me a clean heart", "ref": "Psalm 51:1-10", "leadIn": "This psalm is the prayer of someone who knows they have done wrong and does not hide it. It asks for mercy first, and then for a new heart. Nothing in it tries to earn forgiveness. It asks God to give it.", "prayer": "Merciful God, you know me completely. Wash away what I cannot undo. Create a clean heart in me and make my spirit steady. Amen.", "reflect": "What would it feel like to ask for mercy without making excuses?"}, {"day": 3, "date": "2027-02-12", "week": "Ash Wednesday week: Return to the Lord", "title": "Treasure that lasts", "ref": "Matthew 6:16-21", "leadIn": "Jesus speaks of fasting as something done quietly, for God and not for an audience. He then points to what we treasure, because our hearts follow our treasure. Lent is a good time to ask what we really hold onto.", "prayer": "Father, you see what is done in secret. Help me give up what pulls me away from you, and not to be seen doing it. Let my heart rest in what lasts. Amen.", "reflect": "What gets most of your time and attention? Is that where you want your heart to be?"}, {"day": 4, "date": "2027-02-13", "week": "Ash Wednesday week: Return to the Lord", "title": "Out of the depths", "ref": "Psalm 130", "leadIn": "The psalmist cries out from a very low place and waits for God. The waiting is honest and unhurried. It ends in hope, because with the Lord there is loving kindness and abundant redemption.", "prayer": "Lord, hear my voice. I wait for you more than watchmen wait for the morning. Put my hope in your word and in your love. Amen.", "reflect": "Where in your life are you waiting right now, and what would it mean to wait with hope?"}, {"day": 5, "date": "2027-02-15", "week": "Week 1: Trusting in the wilderness", "title": "Not by bread alone", "ref": "Luke 4:1-4", "leadIn": "After his baptism, Jesus goes into the wilderness and becomes hungry. The first temptation is to meet his own need on his own terms. He answers with scripture: a person does not live by bread alone.", "prayer": "God, you know what I need before I ask. Teach me to trust you when I am hungry or afraid or tired. Let your word feed me today. Amen.", "reflect": "When you feel a need, what is the first thing you reach for?"}, {"day": 6, "date": "2027-02-16", "week": "Week 1: Trusting in the wilderness", "title": "Worship the Lord alone", "ref": "Luke 4:5-8", "leadIn": "The second temptation offers power and glory in exchange for worship. It sounds like a shortcut to a good end. Jesus refuses and says that worship belongs to God alone.", "prayer": "Lord, I am drawn to shortcuts and to being in charge. Keep my loyalty with you. Help me serve you and not only my own plans. Amen.", "reflect": "What do you want so much that it could tempt you to cut a corner?"}, {"day": 7, "date": "2027-02-17", "week": "Week 1: Trusting in the wilderness", "title": "Do not test God", "ref": "Luke 4:9-13", "leadIn": "In the last temptation, the tempter quotes scripture and urges Jesus to prove God’s care by taking a risk. Jesus answers that we should not put the Lord to the test. Trust does not demand proof.", "prayer": "God, I want signs and guarantees. Give me a faith that rests on you instead. Keep me from using your promises for my own ends. Amen.", "reflect": "Where are you asking God for proof when you could be trusting?"}, {"day": 8, "date": "2027-02-18", "week": "Week 1: Trusting in the wilderness", "title": "A refuge and a fortress", "ref": "Psalm 91:1-10", "leadIn": "This psalm speaks of God as a shelter and a fortress for those who trust him. It invites us to make our home in his care. It is a good prayer for a day when we feel exposed.", "prayer": "Lord, you are my refuge. When fear comes, let me run to you first. Under your care I can rest. Amen.", "reflect": "What would change today if you really believed God was your shelter?"}, {"day": 9, "date": "2027-02-19", "week": "Week 1: Trusting in the wilderness", "title": "Taught to depend", "ref": "Deuteronomy 8:1-5", "leadIn": "Jesus’ first answer to the tempter comes from this passage. Israel spent forty years in the wilderness learning to depend on God day by day. The forty days of Lent echo that long walk.", "prayer": "Lord, you led your people through the wilderness and fed them. Teach me to depend on you day by day. Thank you for what you give me today. Amen.", "reflect": "What is God giving you today that you might overlook?"}, {"day": 10, "date": "2027-02-20", "week": "Week 1: Trusting in the wilderness", "title": "The Lord is my shepherd", "ref": "Psalm 23", "leadIn": "After a week of hunger and testing, this psalm brings rest. The shepherd leads, provides and stays close, even in the darkest valley. It is a good prayer to end a week in the wilderness.", "prayer": "Lord, you are my shepherd. Lead me beside quiet water. Walk with me through dark places, and let me dwell in your house. Amen.", "reflect": "Where do you need the shepherd’s guidance this week?"}, {"day": 11, "date": "2027-02-22", "week": "Week 2: Confession and forgiveness", "title": "Happy are the forgiven", "ref": "Psalm 32:1-7", "leadIn": "This psalm describes both the weight of hidden wrongs and the relief of confessing them. Keeping silent left the writer worn out. Confession brought forgiveness and a hiding place.", "prayer": "God of mercy, I do not want to hide from you. Show me what I need to bring into the light. Forgive me and be my hiding place. Amen.", "reflect": "What have you been carrying alone that you could bring to God?"}, {"day": 12, "date": "2027-02-23", "week": "Week 2: Confession and forgiveness", "title": "If we confess", "ref": "1 John 1:5-10", "leadIn": "John says that God is light, and that walking in the light means being honest about ourselves. If we confess our sins, God is faithful and righteous to forgive us. Honesty is where forgiveness starts.", "prayer": "God of light, keep me honest. Show me what I would rather not see. Forgive me and cleanse me, as you promised. Amen.", "reflect": "Is there something you have been calling by a softer name than it deserves?"}, {"day": 13, "date": "2027-02-24", "week": "Week 2: Confession and forgiveness", "title": "Much forgiven, much loved", "ref": "Luke 7:36-47", "leadIn": "At a dinner, a woman known as a sinner washes Jesus’ feet with her tears while the host judges her. Jesus tells a short story about two debtors and says that the one who is forgiven much loves much.", "prayer": "Jesus, you see me as I am. Thank you for forgiving what I could never repay. Let my love for you grow with my gratitude. Amen.", "reflect": "When have you felt deeply forgiven, and how did it change the way you treated others?"}, {"day": 14, "date": "2027-02-25", "week": "Week 2: Confession and forgiveness", "title": "As white as snow", "ref": "Isaiah 1:16-18", "leadIn": "God calls his people to stop doing wrong, learn to do good and seek justice. He then makes an astonishing offer: sins like scarlet can become white as snow. Forgiveness and a changed life belong together.", "prayer": "Lord, wash me and make me clean. Teach me to do good and to seek justice. Thank you for making new what was stained. Amen.", "reflect": "What is one small way you can learn to do good this week?"}, {"day": 15, "date": "2027-02-26", "week": "Week 2: Confession and forgiveness", "title": "Forgive as you were forgiven", "ref": "Colossians 3:12-15", "leadIn": "Paul tells believers to put on compassion, kindness, humility and patience, and to forgive one another as the Lord forgave them. Above all, put on love, which binds everything together.", "prayer": "Lord, you have forgiven me. Soften my heart toward the person I find hard to forgive. Let your peace rule in my heart. Amen.", "reflect": "Is there someone you need to forgive, or someone you need to ask to forgive you?"}, {"day": 16, "date": "2027-02-27", "week": "Week 2: Confession and forgiveness", "title": "Who is a God like you", "ref": "Micah 7:18-19", "leadIn": "Micah ends with praise. God pardons sin and delights in loving kindness. He will tread our iniquities underfoot and cast our sins into the depths of the sea. It is a good place to rest after a week of confession.", "prayer": "God, there is none like you. Thank you for delighting in mercy. Let me leave my sins in the depths and walk free. Amen.", "reflect": "How would your week feel if you believed God delights in showing you mercy?"}, {"day": 17, "date": "2027-03-01", "week": "Week 3: Letting go", "title": "The fast I choose", "ref": "Isaiah 58:6-9", "leadIn": "Isaiah says the fast God wants is more than going without food. It means loosing the bonds of injustice, sharing bread with the hungry and covering the naked. Then, he says, your light will break out like the morning.", "prayer": "God, show me the fast you desire. Free me from what binds me, and move me to help those in need. Let your light rise through my life. Amen.", "reflect": "What could you give up or give away this week that would help someone else?"}, {"day": 18, "date": "2027-03-02", "week": "Week 3: Letting go", "title": "One thing you lack", "ref": "Mark 10:17-22", "leadIn": "A man who has kept the commandments asks what more he needs. Jesus looks at him with love and tells him to sell what he has, give to the poor and follow him. The man goes away sad, because he has great possessions.", "prayer": "Jesus, you look at me with love. Show me what I am holding too tightly. Give me the courage to let go and follow you. Amen.", "reflect": "What would be hardest for you to give up, and why?"}, {"day": 19, "date": "2027-03-03", "week": "Week 3: Letting go", "title": "Rich toward God", "ref": "Luke 12:13-21", "leadIn": "Someone asks Jesus to settle a dispute over an inheritance. Jesus warns against every kind of greed and tells of a farmer who stored up a huge harvest for himself and lost his life that very night. The farmer was not rich toward God.", "prayer": "Lord, you are my true treasure. Loosen the grip that money and possessions have on me. Make me rich toward you. Amen.", "reflect": "If someone watched how you spend your money and time, what would they say you value most?"}, {"day": 20, "date": "2027-03-04", "week": "Week 3: Letting go", "title": "Everything else is loss", "ref": "Philippians 3:7-11", "leadIn": "Paul lists what he once counted as gain and calls it loss compared with knowing Christ. He wants to be found in Christ, with a righteousness that comes through faith and not from his own achievements.", "prayer": "Christ Jesus, knowing you is worth more than anything I own or have achieved. Help me see what I have in the light of you. Amen.", "reflect": "What achievement or label do you lean on to feel secure?"}, {"day": 21, "date": "2027-03-05", "week": "Week 3: Letting go", "title": "Do not worry", "ref": "Luke 12:22-31", "leadIn": "Jesus points to ravens and wildflowers and asks why we worry about food and clothes when God cares for them. He tells his followers to seek God’s kingdom and trust that these needs will be met.", "prayer": "Father, you know what I need. Take my worries today, and teach me to look for your kingdom first. Let me rest in your care. Amen.", "reflect": "What worry can you hand over to God today?"}, {"day": 22, "date": "2027-03-06", "week": "Week 3: Letting go", "title": "A weaned child", "ref": "Psalm 131", "leadIn": "This short psalm pictures a calm soul, like a child resting with its mother. The writer does not chase great things or demand answers. Letting go can mean learning to be quiet.", "prayer": "Lord, quiet my soul. I give up the need to have every answer. Let me rest in you as a child rests, and hope in you always. Amen.", "reflect": "What would it mean to rest today without needing everything figured out?"}, {"day": 23, "date": "2027-03-08", "week": "Week 4: Mercy for others", "title": "What the Lord requires", "ref": "Micah 6:6-8", "leadIn": "Micah asks what offering could ever be enough, and answers plainly: to do justly, love mercy and walk humbly with your God. Faith shows in how we treat people and in how closely we walk with God.", "prayer": "God, make me just, merciful and humble. Keep me from empty gestures. Let my life be a quiet answer to your call. Amen.", "reflect": "Which is hardest for you right now: justice, mercy or humility?"}, {"day": 24, "date": "2027-03-09", "week": "Week 4: Mercy for others", "title": "The good Samaritan", "ref": "Luke 10:25-37", "leadIn": "A lawyer asks who counts as his neighbor. Jesus tells of a Samaritan who stops to help an injured stranger when others pass by. He ends with a question and a command: go and do likewise.", "prayer": "Lord, open my eyes to the person in need near me. Give me time and courage to stop. Make me a neighbor as you have been to me. Amen.", "reflect": "Who do you tend to pass by, and what would stopping look like?"}, {"day": 25, "date": "2027-03-10", "week": "Week 4: Mercy for others", "title": "Love your enemies", "ref": "Matthew 5:43-48", "leadIn": "Jesus asks his followers to love their enemies and pray for those who persecute them. God gives sun and rain to everyone, and we are called to the same wide kindness. It is one of his hardest teachings.", "prayer": "God, you are kind to everyone. Soften my heart toward those I find hard to love. Teach me to pray for them honestly. Amen.", "reflect": "Who is difficult for you to love, and what is one way you could pray for them?"}, {"day": 26, "date": "2027-03-11", "week": "Week 4: Mercy for others", "title": "Be merciful", "ref": "Luke 6:36-38", "leadIn": "Jesus says to be merciful, as our Father is merciful. Do not judge, do not condemn, and forgive. He promises that the measure we give will be the measure we receive.", "prayer": "Merciful Father, keep me from quick judgments. Help me forgive freely and give generously, as you do with me. Amen.", "reflect": "Where have you been quicker to judge than to show mercy?"}, {"day": 27, "date": "2027-03-12", "week": "Week 4: Mercy for others", "title": "Faith that acts", "ref": "James 2:14-17", "leadIn": "James asks what good it is to wish someone well and do nothing when they lack food and clothes. Faith that has no actions is dead by itself. Mercy gives faith its hands.", "prayer": "Lord, let my faith show itself in what I do. Show me one need I can meet today, and help me act on it. Amen.", "reflect": "What is one practical thing you can do this week for someone in need?"}, {"day": 28, "date": "2027-03-13", "week": "Week 4: Mercy for others", "title": "The Lord lifts up", "ref": "Psalm 146:5-9", "leadIn": "The psalm blesses those whose hope is in God. He gives food to the hungry, frees prisoners and preserves the foreigner. When we show mercy, we join in what he is already doing.", "prayer": "Lord, thank you for caring for the hungry, the oppressed and the stranger. Use me to share your care. I put my hope in you. Amen.", "reflect": "How might God use you to join in his care for someone this week?"}, {"day": 29, "date": "2027-03-15", "week": "Week 5: Following Jesus", "title": "Take up your cross", "ref": "Luke 9:23-25", "leadIn": "Jesus says that anyone who wants to follow him must deny themselves and take up their cross daily. He also says that whoever loses their life for his sake will save it. Following him costs something, and it gives life.", "prayer": "Jesus, I want to follow you. Help me set down my own agenda and walk your way today. Give me strength for the cost. Amen.", "reflect": "What would following Jesus look like in one ordinary part of your day?"}, {"day": 30, "date": "2027-03-16", "week": "Week 5: Following Jesus", "title": "Come to me", "ref": "Matthew 11:28-30", "leadIn": "After a hard week of costs, Jesus offers rest. He invites those who are weary and burdened to come to him and to learn from him, gentle and humble in heart.", "prayer": "Jesus, I am tired. I come to you for rest. Teach me your gentle way, and help me carry what you give me. Amen.", "reflect": "What burden are you carrying that you could bring to Jesus today?"}, {"day": 31, "date": "2027-03-17", "week": "Week 5: Following Jesus", "title": "The mind of Christ", "ref": "Philippians 2:1-8", "leadIn": "Paul urges believers to be united in love and to put others first. He holds up Christ, who did not cling to his status but humbled himself, becoming obedient even to death on a cross.", "prayer": "Lord Jesus, you gave yourself for others. Give me your humility. Help me put others first today. Amen.", "reflect": "Who could you serve or put first today?"}, {"day": 32, "date": "2027-03-18", "week": "Week 5: Following Jesus", "title": "A grain of wheat", "ref": "John 12:24-26", "leadIn": "Jesus compares his coming death to a grain of wheat that must fall into the ground to bear fruit. Those who serve him will follow where he goes. Giving ourselves away is how new life grows.", "prayer": "Jesus, teach me to trust that giving myself away brings life. Let my small acts of love bear fruit. I want to serve you. Amen.", "reflect": "What are you holding onto that might bear more fruit if you gave it away?"}, {"day": 33, "date": "2027-03-19", "week": "Week 5: Following Jesus", "title": "A living sacrifice", "ref": "Romans 12:1-2", "leadIn": "Paul asks believers, in view of God’s mercies, to offer their whole lives to God. Instead of fitting the pattern of the world, they are to be transformed by the renewing of their minds.", "prayer": "God of mercy, I offer you my whole life, not just part of it. Renew my mind and shape me to want what you want. Amen.", "reflect": "What part of your life have you not yet offered to God?"}, {"day": 34, "date": "2027-03-20", "week": "Week 5: Following Jesus", "title": "One thing I ask", "ref": "Psalm 27:1-6", "leadIn": "The psalmist says there is one thing he asks above all: to live in God’s presence all his days. With that desire, fear loses its hold. It is a fitting prayer on the day before Holy Week begins.", "prayer": "Lord, you are my light and my salvation. Make your presence the one thing I seek. Give me courage as this week begins. Amen.", "reflect": "What is the one thing you most want right now, and is it what you most need?"}, {"day": 35, "date": "2027-03-22", "week": "Holy Week", "title": "Hosanna", "ref": "Mark 11:1-10", "leadIn": "Yesterday was Palm Sunday. Jesus enters Jerusalem on a young donkey while the crowd spreads cloaks and branches and shouts praise. The King comes humbly, and the week ahead will not be what the crowd expects.", "prayer": "Lord Jesus, you come in humility. Let me welcome you with my whole heart this week. Keep me with you all the way. Amen.", "reflect": "What does it mean to welcome Jesus as king in your own life?"}, {"day": 36, "date": "2027-03-23", "week": "Holy Week", "title": "The hour has come", "ref": "John 12:27-33", "leadIn": "Jesus admits that his soul is troubled, and yet he does not ask to be saved from this hour. He says he came for it. He speaks of being lifted up and drawing all people to himself.", "prayer": "Jesus, you did not turn away from the cross. Be with me when I am troubled. Draw me close to you this week. Amen.", "reflect": "When you are troubled, where do you turn first?"}, {"day": 37, "date": "2027-03-24", "week": "Holy Week", "title": "He carried our sorrows", "ref": "Isaiah 53:1-6", "leadIn": "Isaiah describes a servant who is despised and suffers for others. Christians have long heard this passage as pointing to Jesus. It says he carried our sorrows, and that by his wounds we are healed.", "prayer": "Lord, you carried my griefs. Thank you for taking on what I could not. Let me not look away from your suffering. Amen.", "reflect": "What does it mean to you that someone carried your sorrows?"}, {"day": 38, "date": "2027-03-25", "week": "Holy Week", "title": "Washing feet", "ref": "John 13:3-15", "leadIn": "On the night before he died, Jesus wraps a towel around himself and washes his disciples’ feet. He tells them to do for one another what he has done for them. Love shows itself in humble service.", "prayer": "Jesus, you served even those who would fail you. Make me willing to serve in small, humble ways. Teach me to love as you love. Amen.", "reflect": "Who could you quietly serve today?"}, {"day": 39, "date": "2027-03-26", "week": "Holy Week", "title": "Father, forgive them", "ref": "Luke 23:33-46", "leadIn": "Jesus is crucified between two criminals. He prays for those who crucify him, speaks mercy to the criminal beside him and entrusts himself to the Father. Today we stay with the cross.", "prayer": "Lord Jesus, you forgave even those who wounded you. I am grateful beyond words. Stay with me in this quiet day. Amen.", "reflect": "Take a moment to sit quietly with the cross. What do you want to say to Jesus?"}, {"day": 40, "date": "2027-03-27", "week": "Holy Week", "title": "Waiting at the tomb", "ref": "Matthew 27:57-61", "leadIn": "Joseph of Arimathea lays Jesus’ body in his own new tomb, and a large stone is rolled against the door. The women sit and watch. Today is a day of waiting, with Easter just ahead.", "prayer": "God, the tomb is closed and I wait. Hold me in the silence between the cross and the morning. I trust you with what comes next. Amen.", "reflect": "What does it mean to wait in hope when you cannot yet see the answer?"}], "scripture": {"1": [[12, "“Yet even now,” says the LORD, “turn to me with all your heart,\nand with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning.”", 1], [13, "Tear your heart and not your garments,\nand turn to the LORD, your God;\nfor he is gracious and merciful,\nslow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness,\nand relents from sending calamity.", 0], [14, "Who knows? He may turn and relent,\nand leave a blessing behind him,\neven a meal offering and a drink offering to the LORD, your God.", 0]], "2": [[1, "Have mercy on me, God, according to your loving kindness.\nAccording to the multitude of your tender mercies, blot out my transgressions.", 1], [2, "Wash me thoroughly from my iniquity.\nCleanse me from my sin.", 0], [3, "For I know my transgressions.\nMy sin is constantly before me.", 0], [4, "Against you, and you only, I have sinned,\nand done that which is evil in your sight,\nso you may be proved right when you speak,\nand justified when you judge.", 0], [5, "Behold, I was born in iniquity.\nMy mother conceived me in sin.", 0], [6, "Behold, you desire truth in the inward parts.\nYou teach me wisdom in the inmost place.", 0], [7, "Purify me with hyssop, and I will be clean.\nWash me, and I will be whiter than snow.", 0], [8, "Let me hear joy and gladness,\nthat the bones which you have broken may rejoice.", 0], [9, "Hide your face from my sins,\nand blot out all of my iniquities.", 0], [10, "Create in me a clean heart, O God.\nRenew a right spirit within me.", 0]], "3": [[16, "“Moreover when you fast, don’t be like the hypocrites, with sad faces. For they disfigure their faces that they may be seen by men to be fasting. Most certainly I tell you, they have received their reward.", 1], [17, "But you, when you fast, anoint your head and wash your face,", 0], [18, "so that you are not seen by men to be fasting, but by your Father who is in secret; and your Father, who sees in secret, will reward you.", 0], [19, "“Don’t lay up treasures for yourselves on the earth, where moth and rust consume, and where thieves break through and steal;", 1], [20, "but lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust consume, and where thieves don’t break through and steal;", 0], [21, "for where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.", 0]], "4": [[1, "Out of the depths I have cried to you, LORD.", 1], [2, "Lord, hear my voice.\nLet your ears be attentive to the voice of my petitions.", 0], [3, "If you, LORD, kept a record of sins,\nLord, who could stand?", 0], [4, "But there is forgiveness with you,\ntherefore you are feared.", 0], [5, "I wait for the LORD.\nMy soul waits.\nI hope in his word.", 0], [6, "My soul longs for the Lord more than watchmen long for the morning,\nmore than watchmen for the morning.", 0], [7, "Israel, hope in the LORD,\nfor there is loving kindness with the LORD.\nAbundant redemption is with him.", 0], [8, "He will redeem Israel from all their sins.", 0]], "5": [[1, "Jesus, full of the Holy Spirit, returned from the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into the wilderness", 1], [2, "for forty days, being tempted by the devil. He ate nothing in those days. Afterward, when they were completed, he was hungry.", 0], [3, "The devil said to him, “If you are the Son of God, command this stone to become bread.”", 1], [4, "Jesus answered him, saying, “It is written, ‘Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word of God.’”", 1]], "6": [[5, "The devil, leading him up on a high mountain, showed him all the kingdoms of the world in a moment of time.", 1], [6, "The devil said to him, “I will give you all this authority and their glory, for it has been delivered to me, and I give it to whomever I want.", 0], [7, "If you therefore will worship before me, it will all be yours.”", 0], [8, "Jesus answered him, “Get behind me, Satan! For it is written, ‘You shall worship the Lord your God, and you shall serve him only.’”", 1]], "7": [[9, "He led him to Jerusalem and set him on the pinnacle of the temple, and said to him, “If you are the Son of God, cast yourself down from here,", 1], [10, "for it is written,\n‘He will put his angels in charge of you, to guard you;’", 0], [11, "and,\n‘On their hands they will bear you up,\nlest perhaps you dash your foot against a stone.’”", 1], [12, "Jesus answering, said to him, “It has been said, ‘You shall not tempt the Lord your God.’”", 1], [13, "When the devil had completed every temptation, he departed from him until another time.", 1]], "8": [[1, "He who dwells in the secret place of the Most High\nwill rest in the shadow of the Almighty.", 1], [2, "I will say of the LORD, “He is my refuge and my fortress;\nmy God, in whom I trust.”", 0], [3, "For he will deliver you from the snare of the fowler,\nand from the deadly pestilence.", 0], [4, "He will cover you with his feathers.\nUnder his wings you will take refuge.\nHis faithfulness is your shield and rampart.", 0], [5, "You shall not be afraid of the terror by night,\nnor of the arrow that flies by day,", 0], [6, "nor of the pestilence that walks in darkness,\nnor of the destruction that wastes at noonday.", 0], [7, "A thousand may fall at your side,\nand ten thousand at your right hand;\nbut it will not come near you.", 0], [8, "You will only look with your eyes,\nand see the recompense of the wicked.", 0], [9, "Because you have made the LORD your refuge,\nand the Most High your dwelling place,", 0], [10, "no evil shall happen to you,\nneither shall any plague come near your dwelling.", 0]], "9": [[1, "You shall observe to do all the commandments which I command you today, that you may live, and multiply, and go in and possess the land which the LORD swore to your fathers.", 1], [2, "You shall remember all the way which the LORD your God has led you these forty years in the wilderness, that he might humble you, to test you, to know what was in your heart, whether you would keep his commandments or not.", 0], [3, "He humbled you, allowed you to be hungry, and fed you with manna, which you didn’t know, neither did your fathers know, that he might teach you that man does not live by bread only, but man lives by every word that proceeds out of the LORD’s mouth.", 0], [4, "Your clothing didn’t grow old on you, neither did your foot swell, these forty years.", 0], [5, "You shall consider in your heart that as a man disciplines his son, so the LORD your God disciplines you.", 0]], "10": [[1, "The LORD is my shepherd;\nI shall lack nothing.", 1], [2, "He makes me lie down in green pastures.\nHe leads me beside still waters.", 0], [3, "He restores my soul.\nHe guides me in the paths of righteousness for his name’s sake.", 0], [4, "Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,\nI will fear no evil, for you are with me.\nYour rod and your staff,\nthey comfort me.", 0], [5, "You prepare a table before me\nin the presence of my enemies.\nYou anoint my head with oil.\nMy cup runs over.", 0], [6, "Surely goodness and loving kindness shall follow me all the days of my life,\nand I will dwell in the LORD’s house forever.", 0]], "11": [[1, "Blessed is he whose disobedience is forgiven,\nwhose sin is covered.", 1], [2, "Blessed is the man to whom the LORD doesn’t impute iniquity,\nin whose spirit there is no deceit.", 0], [3, "When I kept silence, my bones wasted away through my groaning all day long.", 0], [4, "For day and night your hand was heavy on me.\nMy strength was sapped in the heat of summer. Selah.", 0], [5, "I acknowledged my sin to you.\nI didn’t hide my iniquity.\nI said, I will confess my transgressions to the LORD,\nand you forgave the iniquity of my sin. Selah.", 0], [6, "For this, let everyone who is godly pray to you in a time when you may be found.\nSurely when the great waters overflow, they shall not reach to him.", 0], [7, "You are my hiding place.\nYou will preserve me from trouble.\nYou will surround me with songs of deliverance. Selah.", 0]], "12": [[5, "This is the message which we have heard from him and announce to you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all.", 1], [6, "If we say that we have fellowship with him and walk in the darkness, we lie and don’t tell the truth.", 0], [7, "But if we walk in the light as he is in the light, we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanses us from all sin.", 0], [8, "If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.", 0], [9, "If we confess our sins, he is faithful and righteous to forgive us the sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.", 0], [10, "If we say that we haven’t sinned, we make him a liar, and his word is not in us.", 0]], "13": [[36, "One of the Pharisees invited him to eat with him. He entered into the Pharisee’s house and sat at the table.", 1], [37, "Behold, a woman in the city who was a sinner, when she knew that he was reclining in the Pharisee’s house, brought an alabaster jar of ointment.", 0], [38, "Standing behind at his feet weeping, she began to wet his feet with her tears, and she wiped them with the hair of her head, kissed his feet, and anointed them with the ointment.", 0], [39, "Now when the Pharisee who had invited him saw it, he said to himself, “This man, if he were a prophet, would have perceived who and what kind of woman this is who touches him, that she is a sinner.”", 0], [40, "Jesus answered him, “Simon, I have something to tell you.” He said, “Teacher, say on.”", 1], [41, "“A certain lender had two debtors. The one owed five hundred denarii, and the other fifty.", 1], [42, "When they couldn’t pay, he forgave them both. Which of them therefore will love him most?”", 0], [43, "Simon answered, “He, I suppose, to whom he forgave the most.” He said to him, “You have judged correctly.”", 1], [44, "Turning to the woman, he said to Simon, “Do you see this woman? I entered into your house, and you gave me no water for my feet, but she has wet my feet with her tears, and wiped them with the hair of her head.", 1], [45, "You gave me no kiss, but she, since the time I came in, has not ceased to kiss my feet.", 0], [46, "You didn’t anoint my head with oil, but she has anointed my feet with ointment.", 0], [47, "Therefore I tell you, her sins, which are many, are forgiven, for she loved much. But one to whom little is forgiven, loves little.”", 0]], "14": [[16, "Wash yourselves. Make yourself clean.\nPut away the evil of your doings from before my eyes.\nCease to do evil.", 1], [17, "Learn to do well.\nSeek justice.\nRelieve the oppressed.\nDefend the fatherless.\nPlead for the widow.”", 0], [18, "“Come now, and let’s reason together,” says the LORD:\n“Though your sins are as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow.\nThough they are red like crimson, they shall be as wool.", 1]], "15": [[12, "Put on therefore, as God’s chosen ones, holy and beloved, a heart of compassion, kindness, lowliness, humility, and perseverance;", 1], [13, "bearing with one another, and forgiving each other, if any man has a complaint against any; even as Christ forgave you, so you also do.", 0], [14, "Above all these things, walk in love, which is the bond of perfection.", 1], [15, "And let the peace of God rule in your hearts, to which also you were called in one body, and be thankful.", 0]], "16": [[18, "Who is a God like you, who pardons iniquity,\nand passes over the disobedience of the remnant of his heritage?\nHe doesn’t retain his anger forever,\nbecause he delights in loving kindness.", 1], [19, "He will again have compassion on us.\nHe will tread our iniquities under foot.\nYou will cast all their sins into the depths of the sea.", 0]], "17": [[6, "“Isn’t this the fast that I have chosen:\nto release the bonds of wickedness,\nto undo the straps of the yoke,\nto let the oppressed go free,\nand that you break every yoke?", 1], [7, "Isn’t it to distribute your bread to the hungry,\nand that you bring the poor who are cast out to your house?\nWhen you see the naked,\nthat you cover him;\nand that you not hide yourself from your own flesh?", 0], [8, "Then your light will break out as the morning,\nand your healing will appear quickly;\nthen your righteousness shall go before you,\nand the LORD’s glory will be your rear guard.", 0], [9, "Then you will call, and the LORD will answer.\nYou will cry for help, and he will say, ‘Here I am.’\n“If you take away from amongst you the yoke,\nfinger pointing,\nand speaking wickedly;", 0]], "18": [[17, "As he was going out into the way, one ran to him, knelt before him, and asked him, “Good Teacher, what shall I do that I may inherit eternal life?”", 1], [18, "Jesus said to him, “Why do you call me good? No one is good except one—God.", 1], [19, "You know the commandments: ‘Do not murder,’ ‘Do not commit adultery,’ ‘Do not steal,’ ‘Do not give false testimony,’ ‘Do not defraud,’ ‘Honour your father and mother.’”", 0], [20, "He said to him, “Teacher, I have observed all these things from my youth.”", 1], [21, "Jesus looking at him loved him, and said to him, “One thing you lack. Go, sell whatever you have and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven; and come, follow me, taking up the cross.”", 1], [22, "But his face fell at that saying, and he went away sorrowful, for he was one who had great possessions.", 1]], "19": [[13, "One of the multitude said to him, “Teacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me.”", true], [14, "But he said to him, “Man, who made me a judge or an arbitrator over you?”", true], [15, "He said to them, “Beware! Keep yourselves from covetousness, for a man’s life doesn’t consist of the abundance of the things which he possesses.”", false], [16, "He spoke a parable to them, saying, “The ground of a certain rich man produced abundantly.", true], [17, "He reasoned within himself, saying, ‘What will I do, because I don’t have room to store my crops?’", false], [18, "He said, ‘This is what I will do. I will pull down my barns, build bigger ones, and there I will store all my grain and my goods.", false], [19, "I will tell my soul, “Soul, you have many goods laid up for many years. Take your ease, eat, drink, and be merry.”’", false], [20, "“But God said to him, ‘You foolish one, tonight your soul is required of you. The things which you have prepared—whose will they be?’", true], [21, "So is he who lays up treasure for himself, and is not rich towards God.”", false]], "20": [[7, "However, I consider those things that were gain to me as a loss for Christ.", 1], [8, "Yes most certainly, and I count all things to be a loss for the excellency of the knowledge of Christ Jesus, my Lord, for whom I suffered the loss of all things, and count them nothing but refuse, that I may gain Christ", 0], [9, "and be found in him, not having a righteousness of my own, that which is of the law, but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness which is from God by faith,", 0], [10, "that I may know him and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings, becoming conformed to his death,", 0], [11, "if by any means I may attain to the resurrection from the dead.", 0]], "21": [[22, "He said to his disciples, “Therefore I tell you, don’t be anxious for your life, what you will eat, nor yet for your body, what you will wear.", 1], [23, "Life is more than food, and the body is more than clothing.", 0], [24, "Consider the ravens: they don’t sow, they don’t reap, they have no warehouse or barn, and God feeds them. How much more valuable are you than birds!", 0], [25, "Which of you by being anxious can add a cubit to his height?", 0], [26, "If then you aren’t able to do even the least things, why are you anxious about the rest?", 0], [27, "Consider the lilies, how they grow. They don’t toil, neither do they spin; yet I tell you, even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.", 0], [28, "But if this is how God clothes the grass in the field, which today exists and tomorrow is cast into the oven, how much more will he clothe you, O you of little faith?", 0], [29, "“Don’t seek what you will eat or what you will drink; neither be anxious.", 1], [30, "For the nations of the world seek after all of these things, but your Father knows that you need these things.", 0], [31, "But seek God’s Kingdom, and all these things will be added to you.", 0]], "22": [[1, "LORD, my heart isn’t arrogant, nor my eyes lofty;\nnor do I concern myself with great matters,\nor things too wonderful for me.", 1], [2, "Surely I have stilled and quieted my soul,\nlike a weaned child with his mother,\nlike a weaned child is my soul within me.", 0], [3, "Israel, hope in the LORD,\nfrom this time forward and forever more.", 0]], "23": [[6, "How shall I come before the LORD,\nand bow myself before the exalted God?\nShall I come before him with burnt offerings,\nwith calves a year old?", 1], [7, "Will the LORD be pleased with thousands of rams?\nWith tens of thousands of rivers of oil?\nShall I give my firstborn for my disobedience?\nThe fruit of my body for the sin of my soul?", 0], [8, "He has shown you, O man, what is good.\nWhat does the LORD require of you, but to act justly,\nto love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God?", 0]], "24": [[25, "Behold, a certain lawyer stood up and tested him, saying, “Teacher, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?”", 1], [26, "He said to him, “What is written in the law? How do you read it?”", 1], [27, "He answered, “You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, with all your soul, with all your strength, and with all your mind; and your neighbour as yourself.”", 1], [28, "He said to him, “You have answered correctly. Do this, and you will live.”", 1], [29, "But he, desiring to justify himself, asked Jesus, “Who is my neighbour?”", 1], [30, "Jesus answered, “A certain man was going down from Jerusalem to Jericho, and he fell amongst robbers, who both stripped him and beat him, and departed, leaving him half dead.", 1], [31, "By chance a certain priest was going down that way. When he saw him, he passed by on the other side.", 0], [32, "In the same way a Levite also, when he came to the place and saw him, passed by on the other side.", 0], [33, "But a certain Samaritan, as he travelled, came where he was. When he saw him, he was moved with compassion,", 0], [34, "came to him, and bound up his wounds, pouring on oil and wine. He set him on his own animal, brought him to an inn, and took care of him.", 0], [35, "On the next day, when he departed, he took out two denarii, gave them to the host, and said to him, ‘Take care of him. Whatever you spend beyond that, I will repay you when I return.’", 0], [36, "Now which of these three do you think seemed to be a neighbour to him who fell amongst the robbers?”", 0], [37, "He said, “He who showed mercy on him.” Then Jesus said to him, “Go and do likewise.”", 1]], "25": [[43, "“You have heard that it was said, ‘You shall love your neighbour and hate your enemy.’", 1], [44, "But I tell you, love your enemies, bless those who curse you, do good to those who hate you, and pray for those who mistreat you and persecute you,", 0], [45, "that you may be children of your Father who is in heaven. For he makes his sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the just and the unjust.", 0], [46, "For if you love those who love you, what reward do you have? Don’t even the tax collectors do the same?", 0], [47, "If you only greet your friends, what more do you do than others? Don’t even the tax collectors do the same?", 0], [48, "Therefore you shall be perfect, just as your Father in heaven is perfect.", 0]], "26": [[36, "“Therefore be merciful,\neven as your Father is also merciful.", 1], [37, "Don’t judge,\nand you won’t be judged.\nDon’t condemn,\nand you won’t be condemned.\nSet free,\nand you will be set free.", 0], [38, "“Give, and it will be given to you: good measure, pressed down, shaken together, and running over, will be given to you. For with the same measure you measure it will be measured back to you.”", 1]], "27": [[14, "What good is it, my brothers, if a man says he has faith, but has no works? Can faith save him?", 1], [15, "And if a brother or sister is naked and in lack of daily food,", 0], [16, "and one of you tells them, “Go in peace. Be warmed and filled;” yet you didn’t give them the things the body needs, what good is it?", 0], [17, "Even so faith, if it has no works, is dead in itself.", 0]], "28": [[5, "Happy is he who has the God of Jacob for his help,\nwhose hope is in the LORD, his God,", 1], [6, "who made heaven and earth,\nthe sea, and all that is in them;\nwho keeps truth forever;", 0], [7, "who executes justice for the oppressed;\nwho gives food to the hungry.\nThe LORD frees the prisoners.", 0], [8, "The LORD opens the eyes of the blind.\nThe LORD raises up those who are bowed down.\nThe LORD loves the righteous.", 0], [9, "The LORD preserves the foreigners.\nHe upholds the fatherless and widow,\nbut he turns the way of the wicked upside down.", 0]], "29": [[23, "He said to all, “If anyone desires to come after me, let him deny himself, take up his cross, and follow me.", 1], [24, "For whoever desires to save his life will lose it, but whoever will lose his life for my sake will save it.", 0], [25, "For what does it profit a man if he gains the whole world, and loses or forfeits his own self?", 0]], "30": [[28, "“Come to me, all you who labour and are heavily burdened, and I will give you rest.", 1], [29, "Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, for I am gentle and humble in heart; and you will find rest for your souls.", 0], [30, "For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.”", 0]], "31": [[1, "If therefore there is any exhortation in Christ, if any consolation of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any tender mercies and compassion,", 1], [2, "make my joy full by being like-minded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind;", 0], [3, "doing nothing through rivalry or through conceit, but in humility, each counting others better than himself;", 0], [4, "each of you not just looking to his own things, but each of you also to the things of others.", 0], [5, "Have this in your mind, which was also in Christ Jesus,", 1], [6, "who, existing in the form of God, didn’t consider equality with God a thing to be grasped,", 0], [7, "but emptied himself, taking the form of a servant, being made in the likeness of men.", 0], [8, "And being found in human form, he humbled himself, becoming obedient to the point of death, yes, the death of the cross.", 0]], "32": [[24, "Most certainly I tell you, unless a grain of wheat falls into the earth and dies, it remains by itself alone. But if it dies, it bears much fruit.", 1], [25, "He who loves his life will lose it. He who hates his life in this world will keep it to eternal life.", 0], [26, "If anyone serves me, let him follow me. Where I am, there my servant will also be. If anyone serves me, the Father will honour him.", 0]], "33": [[1, "Therefore I urge you, brothers, by the mercies of God, to present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable to God, which is your spiritual service.", 1], [2, "Don’t be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind, so that you may prove what is the good, well-pleasing, and perfect will of God.", 0]], "34": [[1, "The LORD is my light and my salvation.\nWhom shall I fear?\nThe LORD is the strength of my life.\nOf whom shall I be afraid?", 1], [2, "When evildoers came at me to eat up my flesh,\neven my adversaries and my foes, they stumbled and fell.", 0], [3, "Though an army should encamp against me,\nmy heart shall not fear.\nThough war should rise against me,\neven then I will be confident.", 0], [4, "One thing I have asked of the LORD, that I will seek after:\nthat I may dwell in the LORD’s house all the days of my life,\nto see the LORD’s beauty,\nand to enquire in his temple.", 0], [5, "For in the day of trouble, he will keep me secretly in his pavilion.\nIn the secret place of his tabernacle, he will hide me.\nHe will lift me up on a rock.", 0], [6, "Now my head will be lifted up above my enemies around me.\nI will offer sacrifices of joy in his tent.\nI will sing, yes, I will sing praises to the LORD.", 0]], "35": [[1, "When they came near to Jerusalem, to Bethsphage and Bethany, at the Mount of Olives, he sent two of his disciples", 1], [2, "and said to them, “Go your way into the village that is opposite you. Immediately as you enter into it, you will find a young donkey tied, on which no one has sat. Untie him and bring him.", 0], [3, "If anyone asks you, ‘Why are you doing this?’ say, ‘The Lord needs him;’ and immediately he will send him back here.”", 0], [4, "They went away, and found a young donkey tied at the door outside in the open street, and they untied him.", 1], [5, "Some of those who stood there asked them, “What are you doing, untying the young donkey?”", 0], [6, "They said to them just as Jesus had said, and they let them go.", 0], [7, "They brought the young donkey to Jesus and threw their garments on it, and Jesus sat on it.", 1], [8, "Many spread their garments on the way, and others were cutting down branches from the trees and spreading them on the road.", 0], [9, "Those who went in front and those who followed cried out, “Hosanna! Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord!", 0], [10, "Blessed is the kingdom of our father David that is coming in the name of the Lord! Hosanna in the highest!”", 0]], "36": [[27, "“Now my soul is troubled. What shall I say? ‘Father, save me from this time’? But I came to this time for this cause.", 1], [28, "Father, glorify your name!” Then a voice came out of the sky, saying, “I have both glorified it and will glorify it again.”", 0], [29, "Therefore the multitude who stood by and heard it said that it had thundered. Others said, “An angel has spoken to him.”", 1], [30, "Jesus answered, “This voice hasn’t come for my sake, but for your sakes.", 1], [31, "Now is the judgement of this world. Now the prince of this world will be cast out.", 0], [32, "And I, if I am lifted up from the earth, will draw all people to myself.”", 0], [33, "But he said this, signifying by what kind of death he should die.", 0]], "37": [[1, "Who has believed our message?\nTo whom has the LORD’s arm been revealed?", 1], [2, "For he grew up before him as a tender plant,\nand as a root out of dry ground.\nHe has no good looks or majesty.\nWhen we see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him.", 0], [3, "He was despised\nand rejected by men,\na man of suffering\nand acquainted with disease.\nHe was despised as one from whom men hide their face;\nand we didn’t respect him.", 0], [4, "Surely he has borne our sickness\nand carried our suffering;\nyet we considered him plagued,\nstruck by God, and afflicted.", 1], [5, "But he was pierced for our transgressions.\nHe was crushed for our iniquities.\nThe punishment that brought our peace was on him;\nand by his wounds we are healed.", 0], [6, "All we like sheep have gone astray.\nEveryone has turned to his own way;\nand the LORD has laid on him the iniquity of us all.", 0]], "38": [[3, "Jesus, knowing that the Father had given all things into his hands, and that he came from God and was going to God,", 1], [4, "arose from supper, and laid aside his outer garments. He took a towel and wrapped a towel around his waist.", 0], [5, "Then he poured water into the basin, and began to wash the disciples’ feet and to wipe them with the towel that was wrapped around him.", 0], [6, "Then he came to Simon Peter. He said to him, “Lord, do you wash my feet?”", 0], [7, "Jesus answered him, “You don’t know what I am doing now, but you will understand later.”", 1], [8, "Peter said to him, “You will never wash my feet!” Jesus answered him, “If I don’t wash you, you have no part with me.”", 1], [9, "Simon Peter said to him, “Lord, not my feet only, but also my hands and my head!”", 1], [10, "Jesus said to him, “Someone who has bathed only needs to have his feet washed, but is completely clean. You are clean, but not all of you.”", 1], [11, "For he knew him who would betray him; therefore he said, “You are not all clean.”", 0], [12, "So when he had washed their feet, put his outer garment back on, and sat down again, he said to them, “Do you know what I have done to you?", 0], [13, "You call me, ‘Teacher’ and ‘Lord.’ You say so correctly, for so I am.", 0], [14, "If I then, the Lord and the Teacher, have washed your feet, you also ought to wash one another’s feet.", 0], [15, "For I have given you an example, that you should also do as I have done to you.", 0]], "39": [[33, "When they came to the place that is called “The Skull”, they crucified him there with the criminals, one on the right and the other on the left.", 1], [34, "Jesus said, “Father, forgive them, for they don’t know what they are doing.” Dividing his garments amongst them, they cast lots.", 1], [35, "The people stood watching. The rulers with them also scoffed at him, saying, “He saved others. Let him save himself, if this is the Christ of God, his chosen one!”", 1], [36, "The soldiers also mocked him, coming to him and offering him vinegar,", 1], [37, "and saying, “If you are the King of the Jews, save yourself!”", 0], [38, "An inscription was also written over him in letters of Greek, Latin, and Hebrew: “THIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.”", 1], [39, "One of the criminals who was hanged insulted him, saying, “If you are the Christ, save yourself and us!”", 1], [40, "But the other answered, and rebuking him said, “Don’t you even fear God, seeing you are under the same condemnation?", 1], [41, "And we indeed justly, for we receive the due reward for our deeds, but this man has done nothing wrong.”", 0], [42, "He said to Jesus, “Lord, remember me when you come into your Kingdom.”", 0], [43, "Jesus said to him, “Assuredly I tell you, today you will be with me in Paradise.”", 1], [44, "It was now about the sixth hour, and darkness came over the whole land until the ninth hour.", 1], [45, "The sun was darkened, and the veil of the temple was torn in two.", 0], [46, "Jesus, crying with a loud voice, said, “Father, into your hands I commit my spirit!” Having said this, he breathed his last.", 0]], "40": [[57, "When evening had come, a rich man from Arimathaea named Joseph, who himself was also Jesus’ disciple, came.", 1], [58, "This man went to Pilate and asked for Jesus’ body. Then Pilate commanded the body to be given up.", 0], [59, "Joseph took the body and wrapped it in a clean linen cloth", 0], [60, "and laid it in his own new tomb, which he had cut out in the rock. Then he rolled a large stone against the door of the tomb, and departed.", 0], [61, "Mary Magdalene was there, and the other Mary, sitting opposite the tomb.", 0]]}};
